.\" Blit server manual. Source of truth for what the binary reads is src/;
.\" tools/tests/documentation_gate.rb fails if a BLIT_ name the code reads
.\" or exports is missing here.
.TH BLIT 8 "2026-10-29" "Blit @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
blit, blit-server \- API-driven native KMS display and terminal server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blit
.RI [ port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blit
drives the machine's displays directly through the Linux kernel's mode
setting (DRM/KMS), with no X11 or Wayland underneath.
It owns the screens, the keyboard, mice and touchpads, and presents
terminal sessions on them: text, colour emoji, Nerd and Blit icon glyphs,
and Kitty and Sixel images.
Everything it does is driven through an HTTP and WebSocket API on
.IR port .
.PP
Blit is the display boundary for the Hibr desktop: Hibr's login manager
and desktops run as terminal sessions inside Blit, and Hibr's Control
Panel configures Blit through the same API as any other client.
Blit does not need Hibr to run; any program can be started in a session.
.PP
Frames are composed on the CPU, or on the GPU through OpenGL ES when that is
chosen; if the GPU cannot be used, the CPU composes instead.
Each display can be split into a grid of panes, each holding one session.
.PP
The package installs the server as
.I /usr/lib/blit/bin/blit-server
with
.I /usr/bin/blit
linking to it, and runs it from
.BR systemd (1)
as
.BR blit.service .
It is normally not started by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I port
TCP port for the API, 1 to 65535.
The default is 8080, which the packaged service also uses.
Any other argument is ignored.
.PP
Everything else is configured through the environment (below) at startup,
and through the API's saved settings document afterwards.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration has two layers.
.IP \(bu 2
The
.B environment
supplies startup values.
The packaged service reads it from
.IR /etc/blit/blit.env ;
see
.BR blit.env (5).
.IP \(bu 2
The
.B settings document
at
.I /var/lib/blit/settings.json
holds what clients saved through
.BR "PUT /v1/settings" :
fonts, pane layout, the compositor, frame timing, pointer and keyboard
settings, effects, the login manager, and the shutdown chord.
A saved value replaces the environment's startup value.
.B "GET /v1/settings"
reports the effective value of each and where it came from;
.B "DELETE /v1/settings"
goes back to the startup values.
.PP
Do not edit the settings document by hand while the server is running:
it is rewritten on every change.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Values marked
.I flag
are on when the first character is
.BR 1 ,
unless stated otherwise.
.SS Network and security
.TP
.B BLIT_AUTH_TOKEN
Bearer token that every API request must send as
.BR "Authorization: Bearer" .
Unset means no authentication, and then the server listens only on
127.0.0.1 unless told otherwise (see the next two entries).
The package generates one at install time.
.TP
.B BLIT_BIND_ADDRESS
IPv4 address to listen on.
Default 0.0.0.0, or 127.0.0.1 when no token is set.
An address that is not IPv4 makes the server exit with status 2.
.TP
.B BLIT_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_NETWORK
.I flag.
Allows a non-loopback
.B BLIT_BIND_ADDRESS
without a token, with a warning.
Without it the server refuses and exits with status 3.
For isolated test networks only.
.TP
.B BLIT_COMMAND_ALLOWLIST
Comma-separated list of the only commands
.B "POST /v1/terminal-sessions"
may run.
Unset or empty allows any command.
.TP
.B BLIT_UPDATE_TOKEN
Token that authorises
.BR "PUT /v1/control/update" ,
which installs a new Blit package.
It is separate from the API token.
Unset means updates through the API are refused.
.TP
.B BLIT_UPDATE_TOKEN_FILE
File holding the update token, used when
.B BLIT_UPDATE_TOKEN
is empty; trailing whitespace is removed.
The package uses
.IR /etc/blit/update.token .
.SS Display and rendering
.TP
.B BLIT_DRM_DEVICE
DRM device to open.
Default
.IR /dev/dri/card0 .
.TP
.B BLIT_DISPLAY_BACKEND
Accepted only as
.BR kms ,
the one backend; any other value is reported as invalid in
.BR /v1/settings .
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_COMPOSITOR
.B gles
composes frames on the GPU; anything else, or unset, uses the CPU.
Saved setting:
.BR server.kms_compositor ,
applied at the next start.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_FRAME_TIMING
.B late
composes each frame as close to the display's refresh as possible, for
lower latency; anything else composes as soon as there is work.
Saved setting:
.BR server.kms_frame_timing ,
applied at once.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_ASYNC_PAGEFLIP
When set to any value, even 0, asks the kernel for asynchronous page flips.
Saved setting:
.BR server.kms_async_pageflip .
.TP
.B BLIT_RENDER_INTERVAL_MS
Render loop interval in milliseconds, 1 to 100; default 16.
Saved setting:
.BR server.render_interval_ms .
.TP
.B BLIT_PANE_LAYOUT
Pane grid on each display at the first start,
.IR C x R
with each of
.I C
and
.I R
1 or 2; default 1x1.
Saved setting:
.BR server.pane_layout ,
also 1x1 to 2x2.
Larger grids, up to 8 by 8, are set per display through the API
.RB ( display_layouts
in the settings document) or Hibr's Control Panel.
.TP
.B BLIT_EXPECT_DESKTOP
.I flag.
Reports a display showing nothing as an error rather than a warning.
Saved setting:
.BR server.expect_desktop .
The package sets it.
.SS Fonts
.TP
.B BLIT_FONT_SCALE
Initial font scale, 1.0 to 3.0 in steps of 0.1; default 1.0.
Fonts are normally chosen by cell height (8 to 64 pixels) through the API.
.TP
.B BLIT_PSF_FONT
Path to a PSF bitmap font used as the startup font.
Default: the bundled Terminus 16 pixel font.
Saved setting:
.BR font.font_id .
.TP
.B BLIT_PSF_WIDE_FONT
PSF font for double-width cells; default the bundled wide font.
.TP
.B BLIT_FONT_ROOT
Directory of the bundled fonts; default
.IR /usr/lib/blit/fonts .
.TP
.B BLIT_FONT_LOCAL_ROOT
Directory of locally installed fonts; default
.IR /usr/local/lib/blit/fonts .
.SS Hibr login manager
.TP
.B BLIT_LOGIN_AUTOSTART
.I flag.
Starts the Hibr login manager on the first display.
Saved setting:
.BR login.enabled .
The package sets it.
.TP
.B BLIT_LOGIN_COMMAND
Hibr binary for the login screen; default
.IR /usr/bin/hibr .
.TP
.B BLIT_LOGIN_SCRIPT
Login wrapper script; default
.IR /usr/share/blit/hibr/blit-login.hibr .
.TP
.B BLIT_LOGIN_SESSION_COMMAND
Command run for the user's session after login; default
.BR "/usr/bin/hibr /usr/share/blit/hibr/blit-login-session.hibr" .
.TP
.B BLIT_LOGIN_DISPLAY_ID
Display the login screen uses; default the first.
.TP
.B BLIT_LOGIN_PANE_ID
Pane the login screen uses.
Saved setting:
.BR login.pane_id .
.SS Input
.TP
.B BLIT_EVDEV_MOUSE
Path of an extra evdev mouse to register at start.
Devices are otherwise found automatically, including when plugged in later.
.SS Settings
.TP
.B BLIT_SETTINGS
.B ignore
starts from the startup values without reading or writing the settings
document: a recovery mode for a document that stops the server starting.
.TP
.B BLIT_SETTINGS_PATH
Where the settings document lives; default
.IR /var/lib/blit/settings.json .
.SS Diagnostics
These print to standard error, which is the journal under systemd.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_TRACE_TIMING
When set, prints overall frame timing.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_TRACE_PHASES
When set, prints the time each output spends in each frame phase.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_FLIP_TIMEOUT_MS
How long to wait for a page flip before giving up on it, 1 to 1000;
default 100.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_CELL_WIDTH
Forces the cell width in pixels, 5 to 32.
.TP
.B BLIT_KITTY_TRACE
When set, logs Kitty graphics replies.
.TP
.B BLIT_TRACE_KEYS
When set, logs keyboard events.
.TP
.B BLIT_TRACE_MOUSE_BUTTONS
When set, logs mouse button events.
.SS Testing
The test suites use these to run the server against fake hardware.
They are not for production use.
.TP
.B BLIT_TEST_MODE
Must be
.B 1
for
.B BLIT_TEST_REFRESH_HZ
to apply.
.TP
.B BLIT_TEST_REFRESH_HZ
Comma-separated refresh rates, one per display, replacing the measured
ones.
.TP
.B BLIT_GLES_PLATFORM
.B surfaceless
runs the GPU compositor without a display and reads frames back.
.TP
.B BLIT_GLES_GUARD_SECONDS
How long a GPU start must stay healthy before its crash guard is
cleared; default 30.
After a crash during a GPU start, the next start uses the CPU.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_MODESET
When set, performs a full mode set on every frame.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_SCREENSHOT_DIR
Directory for a one-time screenshot of each output.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_SCREENSHOT_AFTER
Frame on which that screenshot is taken; default 30.
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_SCREENSHOT_READY_FILE
The screenshot waits until this file exists.
.TP
.B BLIT_INPUT_ROOT
Directory searched for input devices instead of
.IR /dev/input ;
when set, key repeat and device identity are simulated.
.TP
.B BLIT_INPUT_OPEN_DELAY_US
Delay in microseconds before each input device is opened.
.TP
.B BLIT_BACKLIGHT_ROOT
Directory searched for backlights instead of
.IR /sys/class/backlight .
.TP
.B BLIT_ASOUND_ROOT
Directory read instead of
.IR /proc/asound .
.TP
.B BLIT_SND_ROOT
Directory searched for sound devices instead of
.IR /dev/snd ;
when set, mixer controls are simulated.
.TP
.B BLIT_SETTINGS_WRITE_DELAY_MS
Delay before the settings document is written, 0 to 10000; default 0.
.TP
.B BLIT_UPDATE_DIRECTORY
Where uploaded packages are staged; default
.IR /var/lib/blit/updates .
.TP
.B BLIT_UPDATE_SOCKET
Socket of the update helper; default
.IR /run/blit/update.sock .
.TP
.B BLIT_AUXILIARY_LAUNCHER
Script that starts Hibr on the other displays; default
.IR /usr/share/blit/hibr/blit-session.hibr .
.TP
.B BLIT_HIBR_OBSERVER
Script that watches the login desktop; default
.IR /usr/share/blit/hibr/blit-desktop-observe.hibr .
.TP
.B BLIT_HIBR_PLACER
Script that places the other displays' desktops; default
.IR /usr/share/blit/hibr/blit-desktop-place.hibr .
.SS Environment of a session
Every program Blit starts in a session gets
.BR TERM=xterm-kitty ,
.BR COLORTERM=truecolor ,
.B HIBR_GFX=kitty
and
.BR DT_BIDI=on ,
and these:
.TP
.B BLIT_VERSION
The server's version.
.TP
.B BLIT_SERVER_PORT
The API port.
.TP
.B BLIT_API_TOKEN
The API token, when there is one; not given to the login screen.
.TP
.BR BLIT_SESSION_ID ", " BLIT_SESSION_TOKEN ", " BLIT_SURFACE_ID
The session's identity, and a token for its own requests.
.TP
.B BLIT_PANE_ID
The pane the session is in, when it has one.
.TP
.BR BLIT_HIBR_PANE_COL ", " BLIT_HIBR_PANE_ROW
The pane a joining Hibr desktop was asked to start in.
.TP
.B BLIT_VTNR
The virtual terminal Blit holds, so that
.BR systemd-logind (8)
can give a login its seat.
.TP
.BR BLIT_AUDIO_PLAYBACK ", " BLIT_AUDIO_CAPTURE
The default sound devices chosen through the API; playback also sets
.BR ALSA_CARD ,
.B ALSA_PCM_CARD
and
.BR ALSA_PCM_DEVICE .
.TP
.B BLIT_KMS_ASYNC_PAGEFLIP ", " BLIT_KMS_COMPOSITOR
The effective presentation settings.
.TP
.B DT_LOG
For Hibr desktops, a log file under
.I /tmp
unless the request names one.
.PP
A session request may also set
.B BLIT_TERMINAL_FG
and
.B BLIT_TERMINAL_BG
in its environment: the terminal's default foreground and background
colours.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Backspace
Stops the server cleanly; systemd does not restart it.
The chord can be changed or turned off with
.BR "PUT /v1/control/shutdown-key" ,
or from Hibr's Control Panel, and the choice is kept across restarts.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Alt+F1 " ... " F12
Switch to another virtual console, while Blit holds the console.
.PP
To restart the server without a reboot, use
.B "POST /v1/control/restart"
(Restart Blit in Hibr's Control Panel) or
.BR "systemctl restart blit" .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Save settings, release the displays and the console, and exit with
status 0.
.TP
.BR SIGUSR1 ", " SIGUSR2
Used by the kernel to release and reacquire the console when switching
virtual terminals.
.PP
A separate watchdog process restores the console and kills the server if
its main loop stops for 10 seconds.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped by a signal or the shutdown chord.
.TP
.B 1
Could not load a font or open the listener; or exited on purpose after an
update or a failed restart, for systemd to start it again.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid
.I port
or
.BR BLIT_BIND_ADDRESS .
.TP
.B 3
Refused to listen on the network without
.BR BLIT_AUTH_TOKEN .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/blit/blit.env
Startup environment; see
.BR blit.env (5).
.TP
.I /etc/blit/update.token
The update token.
.TP
.I /var/lib/blit/settings.json
The saved settings document.
.TP
.I /var/lib/blit/updates/
Packages uploaded for installation.
.TP
.I /run/blit/update.sock
The update helper's socket; see
.BR blit-update-helper (8).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/blit/fonts/
Bundled fonts, glyph stack, emoji and Blit icons.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/blit/openapi/
The API's OpenAPI description.
.TP
.I /usr/share/blit/hibr/
Scripts that start and place Hibr desktops.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/blit/
The full documentation: start with
.IR README.md ,
.I docs/features.md
and
.IR docs/api.md .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the server, then list displays:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
TOKEN=$(sudo sed -n 's/^BLIT_AUTH_TOKEN=//p' /etc/blit/blit.env)
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/version
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/displays
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start a login shell as the user alice in a session (without
.B user
it runs as the server's own account):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \e
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \e
  -d '{"command":"/bin/bash","arguments":["-l"],"user":"alice"}' \e
  http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/terminal-sessions
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start once without the saved settings, after a bad change:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl stop blit
sudo BLIT_SETTINGS=ignore /usr/bin/blit 8080
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blit.env (5),
.BR blit-update-helper (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR hibr (1)
.PP
